#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><p>
#: news.html:91
msgid ""
"Noteworthy changes in the MLFS system. In addition to the entries in "
"the books changelog, relevant changes you should be aware of are "
"reported here:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dt>
#: news.html:105
msgid "More releases online, change of editorship"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dd>
#: news.html:106
msgid "<em>Zeckma - 2026/02/15</em>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dd><p>
#: news.html:107
msgid ""
"Starting off, there have been efforts for a while to get MLFS "
"rendered in a more official place, have official releases, and have "
"all of them viewable online. That has now finally happened. Releases "
"will now take place alongside LFS's releases, starting with 13.0-rc1 "
"which can be read <a href=\"view/13.0-rc1/\">here</a>. 13.0, when LFS "
"and the other projects release it, will be followed with MLFS-13.0.  "
"For more releases, you can read the <a href=\"index.html\">main page</"
"a> for more details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dd><p>
#: news.html:115
msgid ""
"Editorship has also been changed for months. Thomas Trepl, who "
"maintained MLFS for a long time, stepped down. We thank him for all "
"his work he made on MLFS. I was thus charged in the care of MLFS and "
"have been cleaning various things up. Some of you may have noticed "
"these changes. Stability and cleanliness are the forefront goals of "
"MLFS and most of the work required has now come to pass."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dd><p>
#: news.html:121
msgid ""
"I have various methods of contacting, so if you have any issues with "
"MLFS, you can report them on the <a href=\"/mail.html\">mailing "
"lists</a>, or to my email <a "
"href=\"mailto:zeckma@linuxfromscratch.org\">zeckma@linuxfromscratch.org</"
"a>.  My Discord is also open if that suits you, which is "
"<kbd>@zeckma</kbd> or <kbd>zeckma#0000</kbd>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dd><p>
#: news.html:127
msgid "Happy compiling!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dt>
#: news.html:132
msgid "gcc defaults changed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dd>
#: news.html:133
msgid "<em>Thomas Trepl - 2024/11/12</em>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dd><p>
#: news.html:134
msgid ""
"Added a <kbd>sed</kbd> to all of the gcc build instructions (chapter "
"5, 6, 8) to make the <kbd>-mstackrealign</kbd> flag set by default "
"for the m32 builds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dt>
#: news.html:141
msgid "ISL added"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dd>
#: news.html:142
msgid "<em>Thomas Trepl - long ago</em>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><dl><dd><p>
#: news.html:143
msgid ""
"The package ISL (<a href=\"http://libisl.sourceforge.io/\">see here</"
"a>)  has been added so that gcc will pick it up for some "
"optimizations."
msgstr ""

